# Copy this file to `.env.development.local` before running `npm run dev`:
#
#   cp .env.development.local.example .env.development.local
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS COMMITTED AND WHY COPYING IT MATTERS
#
# Vite layers `.env` -> `.env.development` -> `.env.development.local` per KEY.
# `.env` holds the PRODUCTION values, so any key this file does not set falls
# through to production. Without `.env.development.local` present at all,
# `npm run dev` runs entirely against production: the production Cognito pool
# and the production API URL.
#
# Cognito does not enforce CORS, so that fallback is not harmless. Sign-up and
# sign-in would succeed against the PRODUCTION user pool and create a real user
# there, and only the first API call would fail (on CORS, from localhost). The
# failure arrives after the damage, not before it.
#
# The values below are the dev stack (`BiztrackStack-dev`, CDK). They are real,
# not placeholders, so this file can be copied as-is. None of them are secrets:
# the pool id, app client id and API URL are all shipped inside the public SPA
# bundle already. Never add a password or any real secret to this file - it is
# committed. `.env.development.local` itself stays gitignored.

# ── Cognito: the DEV user pool, never the production one ─────────────────────
VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=ap-south-1_2i6e273DD
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=64okq4elas384cql5dq2jc7ouf
VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN=biztrack-auth-dev.auth.ap-south-1.amazoncognito.com
VITE_APP_URL=https://d2938bm9xnbgsq.cloudfront.net

# ── API: relative, so calls go through the Vite dev proxy ────────────────────
# The deployed API's CORS allowlist trusts only its own CloudFront origin
# (security audit C3). A browser at http://localhost:5173 calling it directly
# gets an opaque CORS failure. `/api` routes calls through the proxy in
# vite.config.ts instead, keeping the browser same-origin so CORS never applies.
VITE_API_URL=/api

# The proxy's real target: the DEV API. vite.config.ts reads this with loadEnv,
# so setting it here works. It previously read process.env, which Vite never
# populates from .env files - that is why this override used to do nothing.
VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=https://gkat4p5bje.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/prod
